# The Wandering Minstrel: "Lands you control enter untapped." Bot1's Ishgard, the Holy See says "This land enters tapped", and
# Bot1, whose land it is, orders the two replacements (CR 616.1): its own first, the Minstrel's last, leaves it untapped
# (the ruling). Bot2's Lindblum, Industrial Regency enters under no Minstrel of Bot2's, so it stays tapped, unasked.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Mox Sapphire
Mox Ruby
The Wandering Minstrel
Ishgard, the Holy See
Wizard's Rockets
Forest x3
Forest x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Lindblum, Industrial Regency
Mountain x3
Mountain x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.The Wandering Minstrel.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Wizard's Rockets.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Ishgard, the Holy See.Play
Bot1.Replace(This land enters tapped)
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ishgard, the Holy See.Tapped = false
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Lindblum, Industrial Regency.Play
[T2 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Ishgard, the Holy See.Tapped = false
Bot2.Battlefield.Lindblum, Industrial Regency.Tapped = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Wizard's Rockets.Tapped = true
